---
const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith("/") ? rawBase : `${rawBase}/`;
const repo = "https://github.com/izzet/quotabubble";
const canonical = new URL(`${base}code-signing/`, Astro.site).href;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Code signing policy — QuotaBubble</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How QuotaBubble's Windows binaries are built and signed, and who is responsible for each step."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href={`${base}favicon.png`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0e0e11" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p class="back"><a href={base}>← QuotaBubble</a></p>
      <h1>Code signing policy</h1>
      <p class="dim">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p>
        Free code signing for QuotaBubble's Windows binaries is provided by
        <a href="https://signpath.org/">SignPath.io</a>, with a certificate issued by the
        <a href="https://signpath.org/">SignPath Foundation</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What is signed</h2>
      <p>
        Only Windows executables that are built from the public source code in
        <a href={repo}>github.com/izzet/quotabubble</a>, by the project's own GitHub Actions release
        workflow, are submitted for signing. Third-party dependencies are not re-signed; they are included
        as published by their upstream authors.
      </p>

      <h2>Roles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Author, reviewer, and approver:</strong>
          <a href="https://github.com/izzet">Izzet Yildirim</a>, the project maintainer. Every change is
          made through a pull request and merged only after review.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Multi-factor authentication is enabled for the maintainer's GitHub and SignPath accounts.
      </p>

      <h2>How a release is signed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A release is triggered by pushing a version tag to the repository.</li>
        <li>The release workflow builds the executable from that tagged source and submits it to SignPath.</li>
        <li>The maintainer approves the signing request, and the signed executable is attached to the GitHub Release.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        QuotaBubble does not send any data to the developer. See the
        <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>privacy policy</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe a signed QuotaBubble binary is malicious or has been tampered with, please open an
        issue at <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>github.com/izzet/quotabubble/issues</a>.
      </p>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <span>MIT licensed</span>
      <span>·</span>
      <a href={repo}>github.com/izzet/quotabubble</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0e0e11;
    --panel: #16161a;
    --line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    --text: #ececf1;
    --dim: #9a9aa5;
    --accent: #5ec584;
  }
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 16px/1.65 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial,
      sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  main {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 24px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 32px 0 8px;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  code {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .dim {
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .back {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .hosts {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .hosts strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  footer {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 24px;
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
